# LeakSanitizer suppressions for `just asan` (docs/audit/2026-09-23-sanitizer-report.md).
# Only leaks that are not ours and that we cannot free belong here. Each entry
# matches any frame of the allocation stack. Keep them narrow enough that a
# leaked mlt++ wrapper of ours still reports (report finding S1): such a
# wrapper is allocated by `new` inside libmlt++/our code, never under
# mlt_factory_producer, so it is not hidden by the entries below.

# MLT's module repository, allocated once by Mlt::Factory::init (fixed ~14 KB).
leak:Mlt::Factory::init
leak:mlt_factory_init

# MLT's loader leaks the normaliser filters it attaches to every producer it
# creates, including the "blank" producer mlt_playlist creates internally
# (report finding S3; upstream). Per-producer and not freeable from our side.
leak:mlt_factory_producer

# SDL audio (via MLT's sdl2_audio consumer, sdl2-compat over SDL3): hint
# cache and mutexes SDL never frees because the audio subsystem is never
# shut down.
leak:libSDL3.so
leak:libSDL2

# App session only (report's "not ours" table): font caches, and AppWindow,
# which main.cpp leaks on purpose for the process lifetime.
leak:libfontconfig.so
leak:libpango
leak:ustudio::app::onActivate

# FFmpeg worker-thread buffers (decode/encode threads spawned via MLT's avformat
# module). `just asan` LD_PRELOADs these libraries so they stay mapped after
# Factory::close() unloads the module and their frames can be symbolized.
leak:libavcodec.so
leak:libavutil.so
leak:libavformat.so
leak:libswscale.so
leak:libswresample.so
leak:libx264.so

# p11-kit's library constructor (newlocale), pulled in by libavformat -> GnuTLS
# when the libraries above are preloaded.
leak:_p11_kit_init

# GDK's display GL setup, reached from gtk_init_check() in the GTK-widget
# tests (dropin-shell): the EGL driver's own state, allocated once per
# process when the display opens and never freed by GTK.
leak:gdk_display_init_egl
